# Run 115 auto-queue cap review repair — RED evidence

Both HOLDs and the availability polish were reproduced as collected behavioural failures.

## HOLD 1: the resolver read the wrong unified-config path
Pre-fix resolver used <runtimeStateRoot>/<scopeId>/runtime-config.yaml, while the host writes
<runtimeStateRoot>/runtime-config.yaml (or legacy <runtimeStateRoot>/state/runtime-config.yaml).
Test: root config daily_cap 7 through the real resolver -> expected 7; pre-fix returned default 100.

## HOLD 2: enabled:false did not bind on non-production channels
Test: limits from dailyCap 0 with enforced:false, reserve one capture -> pre-fix accepted:true.

## Availability polish: replayBudgetAvailable ignored the hard ceiling
Test: ledger status from applyAutoQueueDailyCap({enforced:false}, 0) must expose
hardCounterfactualLimit 0 and replayBudgetAvailable(status) must be false. Pre-fix:
hardCounterfactualLimit was absent from the status object (undefined vs 0) and the availability
check returned true for every unenforced status.

RED commands/results:
- new suite after adding resolver/non-production assertions: 3 failed | 7 passed (10)
  (resolver default 100, hard field missing, disabled reservation accepted)
- after adding the availability assertion: 1 failed | 12 passed (13)
  (hardCounterfactualLimit undefined; availability not consulted)
